answers.body:
I don't know exactly what your homework means by parallelize along row and column but I know why your code is not working.  You have a race condition when you write to v2[i] .  You can fix it by making private versions of v2[i] , filling them in parallel, and then merging them with a critical section. #pragma omp parallel
{
    float v2_private[tam] = {};
    int i,j;
    for (i = 0; i < tam; i++) {
        #pragma omp for
        for (j = 0; j < tam; j++) {
            v2_private[i] += matrix[i][j] * v1[j];
        }
    }
    #pragma omp critical
    {
        for(i=0; i<tam; i++) v2[i] += v2_private[i];
    }
} I tested this.  You can see the results here http://coliru.stacked-crooked.com/a/5ad4153f9579304d Note that I did not explicitly define anything shared or private.  It's not necessary to do.  Some people think you should explicitly define everything.  I personalty think the opposite.  By defining i and j (and v2_private ) inside the parallel section they are made private.

I'd say the row version is more efficient because there is no private storage required for each thread and there is no need to use critical section or mutex for partial summation.
The code is also much simpler: #pragma omp parallel for
for (int i = 0; i < tam; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < tam; j++) {
        v2[i] += matrix[i][j] * v1[j];
    }
}

