Here's straight c++ code that runs in .08s with ints and .14s with floats or doubles. My system is 10 years old with relatively slow memory. Good at the time but now is now. I agree with @VictorEijkhout that the best results would be with tuned code. There has been huge amounts of work optimizing those. #include <vector>
#include <array>
